## Phase 1: CSS Architecture Refactoring

> **Goal**: Untangle the CSS spaghetti. Create a clean separation between desktop and mobile so future iterations on either don't break the other.

### File Changes

#### [MODIFY] [style.css](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/core/css/style.css)

1. **Extract all `@media` blocks** scattered throughout — move them to the bottom of the file in a single organized `/* ========== RESPONSIVE OVERRIDES ========== */` section, **BUT** only for minor tweaks (font sizes, padding)
2. **Remove any mobile-specific layout rules** from `style.css` — these belong in the mobile file
3. **Add CSS custom properties for motion** to `:root`:
   ```css
   --spring: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
   --ease-smooth: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
   --duration-fast: 0.2s;
   --duration-normal: 0.4s;
   --duration-slow: 0.8s;
   --accent-warm: #FF6B35;
   ```
4. **Consolidate duplicate selectors** — there are multiple `.nav-link::after` definitions, multiple `.filter-btn.active` blocks, etc.

#### [NEW] [mobile-v2.css](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/core/css/mobile-v2.css)

A complete mobile stylesheet that replaces both `mobile.css` and the inline `<style id="mobile-force-overdrive">` in `index.html`. Architecture:

```css
/* ============================================
   MOBILE ARCHITECTURE v2.0
   Breakpoints:
     - Tablet:  max-width: 1024px
     - Phone:   max-width: 768px
     - Small:   max-width: 480px
   ============================================ */

/* Tablet (≤1024px) */
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  /* Navigation → hamburger */
  /* Hero grid → single column */
  /* Cards/grids → single column stacking */
  /* Terminal → progressive disclosure */
  /* Bottom dock → visible */
}

/* Phone (≤768px) */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  /* Hero profile card downsized */
  /* Typography scaled down */
  /* Padding/margins compressed */
  /* Timeline → horizontal scroll snap */
}

/* Small Phone (≤480px) */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  /* Further size reductions */
  /* Single-column everything */
}
```

**Key rules**:
- **No `!important`** — achieve specificity through proper selector nesting (e.g., `body .hero-grid` instead of `html body .hero-grid { ... !important }`)
- **No layout rules in desktop CSS** dependent on mobile — each file is self-contained
- **Use `clamp()` and `min()`** for fluid sizing instead of hard breakpoints where possible

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///Users/vineetkishore/Documents/iCloud%20Drive/Drive%20X/Softwares/Coding%20Projects/Portfolio%20Project/index.html)

1. Remove the inline `<style id="mobile-force-overdrive">` block (lines 57–166)
2. Replace `<link rel="stylesheet" href="core/css/mobile.css">` with `<link rel="stylesheet" href="core/css/mobile-v2.css">`

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Keep `mobile.css` and `mobile-overhaul.css.bak` in the filesystem as backups, but they should NOT be linked in the HTML.

