## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Blog file structure**: The plan proposes `blogs/index.json` as a manually-maintained manifest. The user must add new posts to this JSON file when publishing. An alternative is to auto-discover `.md` files using GitHub API — but since this is a static site on GitHub Pages without a build step, the JSON manifest is the simplest approach. **Does this work for you?**

> [!WARNING]
> **CSS Architecture Reset**: Phase 1 removes the inline `<style id="mobile-force-overdrive">` and replaces `mobile.css` with `mobile-v2.css`. This is a clean break from the `!important` approach. During development, there may be a brief period where mobile styles are unstable before `mobile-v2.css` is complete. The old files will be kept as backups.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Extras Assets**: Several unused images in `extras/` could enhance the site. The plan uses a few of them judiciously. If you prefer to keep the site lean and skip the extras, let me know.

