## Verification Plan

### Automated / Browser Verification

#### 1. Desktop Visual Checks (Browser)
- Open `index.html` in browser at **1440×900** viewport
- Verify: Preloader → Hero entrance → scroll through all sections
- Check: section transitions are smooth, no visual glitches
- Check: Project filters work (clicking filters shows/hides cards)
- Check: Project Nexus modal opens and closes
- Check: Terminal is interactive and functional
- Check: Contact card click shows toast notification

#### 2. Mobile Visual Checks (Browser at 390×844, iPhone 14 Pro)
- Verify: Hamburger menu visible and functional
- Verify: Bottom dock visible, items tappable, active state updates on scroll
- Verify: Hero section: text readable, image below text, CTAs side-by-side
- Verify: All card sections stack vertically, no horizontal overflow
- Verify: Timeline cards stack vertically
- Verify: No horizontal scrollbar on any section
- Verify: Terminal teaser visible, tappable to reveal terminal

#### 3. Blog Engine Checks (Browser)
- Navigate to `blog.html` — verify 3 sample posts render as cards
- Click pagination (with 3 posts there should be 1 page — test with 15+ posts later)
- Test sort: Latest → Oldest  
- Click on a blog card → verify `blog-post.html?slug=...` loads
- Verify markdown renders: headings, code blocks, lists, bold, italic, links, tables, blockquotes
- Press "← Back to Blog" → returns to listing
- Check blog pages on mobile (390px) — verify responsive layout

### Manual Verification (by user)
1. Deploy to GitHub Pages and verify all links and asset loading work with relative paths
2. Add a new `.md` file to `blogs/`, update `index.json`, and verify it appears on the listing page
3. Test on a real iPhone / Android device for touch responsiveness
